    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0525" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg443"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to the Marquis de Montholon</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 31, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 19th instant in regard to violation of neutrality of the
                    United States alleged to have taken place recently on the Rio Grande. In reply,
                    I have the honor to inform you that I have requested the Secretary of War to
                    cause the matter to be inquired into with a view to the adoption of such
                    proceedings as may be called for.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, a renewed assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marquis de Montholon</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
